    <!-- 8 COMPLETE vs INCOMPLETE COMBUSTION (8.7-8.10) -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="combustion">
      <span class="tag lo">Combustion · 8.7–8.10</span>
      <h2>Complete vs incomplete combustion</h2>
      <p>Burning a hydrocarbon fuel is <b>combustion</b> — and it releases energy. What it produces depends on how much <b>oxygen</b> is available:</p>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 230" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Complete combustion gives carbon dioxide and water; incomplete combustion gives carbon monoxide, carbon soot and water">
          <!-- complete -->
          <rect x="14" y="14" width="262" height="200" rx="16" fill="#eafaf0" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="145" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#137a45">Complete</text>
          <text x="145" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="11.5" fill="#137a45">plenty of oxygen</text>
          <text x="145" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#2c2840">fuel + O₂ →</text>
          <g font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" font-weight="600">
            <rect x="40" y="108" width="92" height="34" rx="9" fill="#d6f6e4" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/><text x="86" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#137a45">CO₂</text>
            <rect x="158" y="108" width="92" height="34" rx="9" fill="#dcecff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/><text x="204" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0b5bbf">H₂O</text>
          </g>
          <text x="145" y="172" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="11.5" fill="#137a45">carbon dioxide + water</text>
          <text x="145" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#137a45">clean blue flame</text>
          <!-- incomplete -->
          <rect x="284" y="14" width="262" height="200" rx="16" fill="#fdeef0" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="415" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#c8203a">Incomplete</text>
          <text x="415" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="11.5" fill="#c8203a">not enough oxygen</text>
          <text x="415" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#2c2840">fuel + less O₂ →</text>
          <g font-family="Fredoka" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600">
            <rect x="298" y="108" width="74" height="34" rx="9" fill="#ffd6d9" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/><text x="335" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c8203a">CO</text>
            <rect x="378" y="108" width="74" height="34" rx="9" fill="#e0ddd6" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/><text x="415" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3a3550">C (soot)</text>
            <rect x="458" y="108" width="74" height="34" rx="9" fill="#dcecff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/><text x="495" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0b5bbf">H₂O</text>
          </g>
          <text x="415" y="172" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="11" fill="#c8203a">carbon monoxide + carbon + water</text>
          <text x="415" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#c8203a">smoky orange flame</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>With plenty of O₂ you get <b>CO₂ + H₂O</b>. With too little O₂ you also get <b>carbon monoxide (CO)</b> and <b>carbon (soot)</b>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="note"><b>Misconception fix:</b> incomplete combustion does <b>not</b> just make "less CO₂" — it makes <b>different products</b>: toxic <b>carbon monoxide</b> and <b>soot</b>. CO is dangerous because it is <b>colourless and odourless</b> and binds to haemoglobin in the blood, stopping it carrying oxygen. Soot blackens appliances and can cause breathing problems.</p>
    </section>

