      <h2>The ideas to know</h2>
      <div class="recap">
        <p><b>Crude oil:</b> finite <b>mixture</b> of hydrocarbons, split by <b>physical</b> distillation.</p>
        <p><b>Alkanes:</b> C<sub>n</sub>H<sub>2n+2</sub> — methane, ethane, propane, butane.</p>
        <p><b>Down the column:</b> longer chain → higher boiling point &amp; viscosity, harder to ignite.</p>
        <p><b>Complete:</b> CO₂ + H₂O. <b>Incomplete:</b> CO (toxic) + carbon (soot) + H₂O.</p>
        <p><b>Pollutants:</b> SO₂ (sulfur impurities) &amp; NOₓ (N₂+O₂ in hot engines) → <b>acid rain</b>.</p>
        <p><b>Cracking:</b> long alkanes → shorter alkanes + <b>alkenes</b> (supply &amp; demand).</p>
        <p><b>Hydrogen fuel:</b> clean (only water) but hard to store; petrol is convenient but polluting.</p>
        <p><b>Atmosphere:</b> volcanic CO₂/water vapour → CO₂ <b>fell</b>, O₂ <b>rose</b>; now ~78% N₂, ~21% O₂.</p>
        <p><b>Greenhouse gases:</b> CO₂, methane, water vapour — natural &amp; needed; humans enhance the effect.</p>
